      "content": "Got it. To see if I'm understanding the pattern correctly, let's look at a second case that's very similar but has a different background.\n\nCase 2:\nDefendant: William Sterling\nCharge: Possession of 50g of cocaine with intent to distribute.\nCircumstances: Arrested during a traffic stop in a quiet suburban neighborhood. No prior violent criminal record, but two prior misdemeanor drug possession charges. Defendant is currently a freelance consultant and resides in a single-family owned home.\n\nHow would the sentencing recommendation and the judicial weight of the factors change for Mr. Sterling compared to Mr. Washington?",
